      "writtenOn": "2017-07-19T14:07:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is not true, as explained above. There is still a default rule, we\u0027re just not configuring a default value for it because we don\u0027t care about/use it. If an operator is extending keystone APIs with their own custom APIs, or monkey-patching keystone code to do additional policy checks, or something funky like that, and they don\u0027t code default values for those checks they are introducing, they may (and still can) want to use the default rule. But that\u0027s totally on them and not something we care about or need to address.",
